quired result now using this  result we can rewrite  the 2l plus 1 double factorial as equal  to this for the second result  consider an even number m equal to 2k  for some other integer k then m  double factorial is equal to 2 to the  power of k  times the factorial of k and again  this is easy to understand because the  factorial over k starts from half the  value of  m and then multiplying each term by 2  gives the proper m sequence and we have  k  such terms so using this result  for 2l double factorial we get this  and we're now ready to go back to il  if we first use this expression for the  denominator we get  this we can then use this expression for  the numerator  and we get this  and simplifying we get this result  and now we can finally go back to our  normalization factor cl up here  and we can now write it in terms of this  later result that we got  taking the square root of both sides and  reorganizing somewhat  we get that the absolute value of c l is  equal to  1 over 2 to the l times l factorial  multiplying the square root of 2 l plus  1 factorial divided by 4 pi  cl is in principle a complex number so  we still have to determine its face  this face choice is of course arbitrary  because we only ever get  the absolute value squared of this  quantity  in quantum mechanics so we could in  principle pick  any value for the face the usual  convention though is to make a face  choice such that even and odd values of  l have a different sign so finally we  get  cl equal to this  and this time we really are done  this is the expression for cl that we  used earlier on  to build the full expression for the m  equals l  spherical harmonic  spherical harmonics are the eigen  functions of orbital angular momentum  although their mathematical form is not  particularly simple  they are very important in many systems  for example the hydrogen atom spherical  harmonics are also rather beautiful when  visualized  so i really encourage you to check them  out and as 